!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Liver
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Liver
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue preservation method: FFPE
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: CRLM tumor
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample identifier: M242T
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = tissue preparation protocol: The samples were sectioned at 5µm thickness and placed onto Xenium slides. This was followed by deparaffinization, rehydration, and decrosslinking of the tissue sections.
!Sample_label_ch1 = Xenium probe set
!Sample_label_protocol_ch1 = Xenium probe set
!Sample_hyb_protocol = Probe hybridization was carried out overnight at 50°C according to manufacturer's protocol either using a 462-gene (Tumor 1, Tumor 2, and Adjacent Normal) or a 319-gene (Tumor 3) Xenium Standalone Custom panel, followed by ligation, and rolling circle amplification. Cell segmentation staining was performed using Xenium Multi-Tissue Stain Mix, followed by autofluorescence quenching and nuclei staining.
!Sample_scan_protocol = The tissue sections were imaged on 10x Genomics Xenium In Situ Analyzer.
!Sample_description = CRLM tumor tissue section, Xenium spatial transcriptomics performed using a 462-gene panel.
!Sample_data_processing = Raw data was processed using the Xenium Onboard Analysis software.
